        {
            "number": 4,
            "revision": "88c111f7cf7c378832050ee5dff009dc898e678e",
            "parents": [
                "b7038188e329343d99bca0ceb3d1472e5e5693bd"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/89/90789/4",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                "username": "ojayanth"
            },
            "createdOn": 1780890838,
            "author": {
                "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                "username": "ojayanth"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 17,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think these can be simultaneously true?\n\nI'm of the opinion that CPERs should have their own interface.  I don't understand what we get by muxing every concieveable logging format into a single DBus interface, other than a complex, confusing implementation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "The proposed scheme here seems to be, read this property to decide how to interpret the reset of the interface.  Why not just make a new interface?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. The idea is not to change how the interface works, but to keep Logging.Entry as one common place for all events, and use the property only to classify them.\nIf we split into multiple interfaces, clients would need to handle multiple event types separately as new ones are added. Keeping one interface keeps things simple and stable.\n\u2019m not completely against moving to a separate interface if that\u2019s considered a cleaner approach .  @Ptarick @Matt please add your thoughts here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 114,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I feel like a separate interface may be better.  That way, it could only be created if necessary.  We also wouldn't have to worry about what DiagnosticType should be set to for non CPER-type logs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "Are we leaking HTTP into our abstraction layer?  It seems like this should be a file descriptor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "The busctl tool has some issue with file descriptors, though I can't remember exactly what it is.  It's possible that it won't display them, and if that's the case I think we would need to talk about if we'd want to end busctl support for logging, which I don't think we do."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Entry.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I think it was just using it as a method call param that was the problem"
                }
            ],
