                "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                "username": "ojayanth"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/CPER.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brad Bishop",
                        "email": "bradleyb@fuzziesquirrel.com",
                        "username": "bradbishop"
                    },
                    "message": "What's the interface on this object?\n\nWouldn't it be simpler to provide access to the data here, rather than through this indirection?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/CPER.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 36,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks \u2014 that\u2019s a good point. The intent here is to avoid carrying large CPER payloads in DiagnosticInfo, while still allowing access to full diagnostic data when needed.\nSince we already point to OpenBMC-managed objects (like dump entries), would adding a line about the referenced object exposing data through a well-defined interface improve clarity here?"
                }
            ],
