            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Diagnostic/CPER.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "sandeepsanku",
                        "username": "sandeepsanku"
                    },
                    "message": "Can this be string type similar to \"Data\" property at https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/+/90374/10/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/State/Cper.events.yaml\n? \nIf there are any sections that doesn't fit dict[string, variant[string, uint64, boolean]] structure, then additional handling has to be done both in phosphor logging and in bmcweb."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Diagnostic/CPER.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a valid concern with the current dict<string, variant<string, uint64, boolean>> approach, especially for CPER where the data is inherently nested and not always representable within this limited type set.\nI've initiated a discussion here to get broader feedback:\nhttps://discord.com/channels/775381525260664832/1511793585127690340/1516262010696892416\nOne possible direction is to align with the Data property pattern used in Cper.events.yaml, i.e., represent this as a JSON string, which avoids lossy transformations and preserves full CPER structure.\nOtherwise, as mentioned, any sections that don\u2019t fit the current dictionary model would require custom handling in both phosphor-logging and bmcweb, which could increase complexity and maintenance overhead.\nBased on  feedback from the discussion and update the approach accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Diagnostic/CPER.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 20,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jayanth Othayoth",
                        "email": "ojayanth@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ojayanth"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
            ],
